{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is scored exactly once with the built-in `neg_binomial_2_log` distribution using a plain sampling statement. The other data variables (`M`, `N`, `x0`, and `X`) are context inputs used only for dimensions and predictors. Each parameter (`alpha`, `beta`, and `inv_phi`) has exactly one built-in prior sampling statement before the observation model uses it.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> M; // Number of covariates
  int<lower=0> N; // Number of observations

  vector[M] x0;   // Covariate baselines
  matrix[N, M] X; // Covariate design matrix

  array[N] int y;      // Variates
}

transformed data {
  matrix[N, M] deltaX;
  for (n in 1:N) {
    deltaX[n,] = X[n] - x0';
  }
}

parameters {
  real alpha;            // Intercept
  vector[M] beta;        // Slopes
  real<lower=0> inv_phi; // Dispersion parameter
}

transformed parameters {
  // inv_phi = 0, phi = +infty reduces to initial Poisson model
  real<lower=0> phi = 1 / inv_phi;
}

model {
  // Prior model
  alpha ~ normal(3, 0.2);
  beta ~ normal(0, log(1.28));
  inv_phi ~ normal(0, 1); // Expand around initial Poisson model

  // Vectorized observation model
  y ~ neg_binomial_2_log(alpha + deltaX * beta, phi);
}

// Simulate a full observation from the current value of the parameters
generated quantities {
  vector[N] mu = exp(alpha + deltaX * beta);
  array[N] int y_pred = neg_binomial_2_log_rng(alpha + deltaX * beta, phi);
}
